NNAAMMEE
     eellffdduummpp — display information about ELF files

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     eellffdduummpp --aa | --EE | --ccddeeGGhhiinnpprrss [--ww _f_i_l_e] _f_i_l_e

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The eellffdduummpp utility dumps various information about the specified ELF
     _f_i_l_e.

     The options are as follows:

     --aa       Dump all information.

     --cc       Dump section headers.

     --dd       Dump dynamic symbols.

     --ee       Dump ELF header.

     --EE       Return success if _f_i_l_e is an ELF file and failure if it is not.
              This option is exclusive with other options.

     --GG       Dump the GOT.

     --hh       Dump the hash values.

     --ii       Dump the dynamic interpreter.

     --nn       Dump note sections.

     --pp       Dump the program header.

     --rr       Dump relocations.

     --ss       Dump the symbol table.

     --ww _f_i_l_e  Write output to a _f_i_l_e instead of the standard output.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The eellffdduummpp utility exits 0 on success, and >0 if an error occurs.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     The following is an example of a typical usage of the eellffdduummpp command:

           elfdump -a -w output /bin/ls

